### Finding 20: export filename truncation splits surrogate pair
(reported by independent auditors; duplicates merged — treat them as one finding and satisfy all of them)

- [P3] [A] Export file name truncation can split a surrogate pair and produce very long paths — lib/services/download/download_service.dart:666-695
  `substring(0, 120)` counts UTF-16 units, so an emoji at the boundary leaves a lone surrogate. Folder name plus file name repeat the ≤120-char title twice. On Windows without long-path support this may pass 260 characters and make the merge fail back to m4s. The Windows part is a **hypothesis**.

In addition, the user picked routes for seven findings that were deferred; the fixer implemented them as R1-R7. Evaluate each against its stated requirement:

## R1 (pass1-D1) — deleting a download vs the exported mp4 folder
Finding: deleteDownload/deletePage call `_deleteMerged`, which recursively deletes the user-visible exported folder `Download/LibrePili/<title>/` (lib/services/download/download_service.dart ~604-724).
User's pick: the delete confirmation dialog offers an option "同时删除导出的视频文件" (also delete the exported file). Default state of the option: unchecked (deleting user files is irreversible). When unchecked, remove the in-app entry and the internal cache only; the exported folder stays. Cover every delete entry point (single entry, whole page, multi-select if any).

## R2 (pass1-D2) — self-test isolation
Finding: `--selftest` runs against the real user profile and deletes existing downloads (lib/utils/self_test.dart ~328-374, 444-447).
User's pick: give the self-test its own data directory and its own download directory, so it never reads or deletes the user's Hive boxes or downloads. Decide the mechanism (e.g. when `--selftest` is in the launch args, point the app data/Hive path and the download root at a `selftest` subfolder before storage init). The destructive "clean state" steps must then only ever touch the isolated dirs.

## R3 (pass1-D4) — old single-URL (Type1) downloads
Finding: mediaType==1 downloads are only moved/renamed to `<name>.mp4` whatever their real format (`response.format`, can be FLV), only the first segment is downloaded, and the media scan tags it video/mp4 (download_service.dart ~556-570, http/download.dart ~203).
User's pick: remux FLV to a real mp4. Implement a pure-Dart FLV demuxer (H.264/AVC video + AAC audio tags; parse AVCDecoderConfigurationRecord / AudioSpecificConfig from the sequence-header tags; composition time offsets) feeding a progressive mp4 writer — reuse lib/utils/mp4_remux.dart's writer pieces where it fits instead of duplicating box writing. Also download ALL segments (not just the first) and join them in timeline order into the single mp4. If a stream is already mp4, keep the existing path. If the codec is something you cannot remux (e.g. not AVC/AAC), keep the original file with its true extension and correct MIME, and say so. Add unit tests for the FLV demux on a small synthetic FLV built in the test (test/ is gitignored; add with the file anyway, the orchestrator will force-add).

## R4 (pass1-D5) — offline comments and images
Finding: LocalReplyPanel loads avatars over the network (lib/pages/video/reply/local_reply_panel.dart ~132-137).
User's pick: avatars → a local placeholder, no network. BUT images inside comments must be downloaded with the download: picture attachments on comments and replies, and the emote images used in comment text. Save them into the video's folder (e.g. a `comments_images/` subfolder, deduplicated by URL hash), record the local relative path in the comments JSON, and render them from local files in LocalReplyPanel. The offline panel must make zero network requests. Respect the existing comment-count settings; images are part of the "comments" extra (no separate toggle unless trivial).

## R5 (pass1-D6) — hide-interaction scope
Finding: the "隐藏发评论与发弹幕" switch only gates the video page; dynamic, article (opus/专栏) and live comment/danmaku-writing entry points are not covered (setting text at lib/pages/setting/models/extra_settings.dart:133; existing gates at reply/view.dart:125, reply_item_grpc.dart:514, video/view.dart:1399, header_control.dart:1861).
User's pick: gate the other entry points too. Sweep the WHOLE app for every UI that writes a comment/reply or sends danmaku/live chat (dynamic detail, article/opus, live room input, music/audio, pgc, member pages, anything else you find) and hide it when the switch is on — and also when not logged in (project rule: login-only interactive controls are hidden when logged out). Comments must still DISPLAY normally; only writing UI is hidden. List every entry point you gated.

## R6 (pass1-D7) — iOS/macOS/Linux identifiers
Finding: Linux APPLICATION_ID `com.example.piliplus`, macOS/iOS bundle ids and app names, and linux/macos/ios CI artifact names are still upstream, so these builds cannot coexist with the original PiliPlus.
User's pick: rename them, following what Windows/Android already use in this branch (grep for `librepili`/`LibrePili` in windows/, android/, .github/ to match the exact id and display name). Cover bundle id, display/product name, Linux binary + desktop/app id, and workflow artifact names. Do not touch signing/provisioning secrets.

## R7 — analyzer warnings
`dart analyze` reports 5 unused imports in lib/http/live.dart, lib/http/video.dart, lib/pages/audio/view.dart, lib/pages/mine/controller.dart (x2); all are fork-touched files. Remove them if they are genuinely unused.



